From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:42:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: sleep: let the command line cap the S2R
 mailbox size

With aura r8's Stage 2, which publishes a 0x98-byte mailbox, a kernel 1.872
trial boot reset the Mac after the kernel had started. The kernel's
only difference under r8 is that apple-sleep maps 0x98 bytes of the
mailbox instead of 32 and allocates the 4 KiB DRAM-check page.

apple_sleep.mbox_size_max=0x20 makes the kernel behave as it does with
an older aura, so a single trial boot of the same Stage 2 tells the
kernel's part from aura's. The default uses what aura publishes.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c b/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
index 66ba926658..5375cb54d2 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
@@ -4092,6 +4092,12 @@ static int apple_sleep_map_regs(struct apple_sleep *s)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* Bring-up: the most of the mailbox to use; 0x20 behaves as before aura r7. */
+static unsigned int mbox_size_max = AURA_S2R_SLC_SIZE;
+module_param(mbox_size_max, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(mbox_size_max,
+		 "Bring-up: use at most this much of aura's S2R mailbox (0x20: as before aura r7)");
+
 static int apple_sleep_map_mailbox(struct apple_sleep *s)
 {
 	struct device_node *chosen;
@@ -4106,6 +4112,7 @@ static int apple_sleep_map_mailbox(struct apple_sleep *s)
 	ret = of_property_read_u64(chosen, "aurora,s2r-mailbox", &pa);
 	if (of_property_read_u32(chosen, "aurora,s2r-mailbox-size", &size))
 		size = 0;
+	size = min(size, mbox_size_max);
 	of_node_put(chosen);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_info(s->dev, "no aurora,s2r-mailbox from the boot object: no deep sleep\n");
-- 
2.43.0

